                <pb facs="0928" n="816" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg816"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2491/130A.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister for Foreign Affairs of Costa
                        Rica.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The convention of arbitration was signed last evening by the representatives of
                    Costa Rica and Panama. I congratulate you and your Government most cordially
                    upon this honorable and satisfactory solution of an old and troublesome
                    question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
